# TypeScript Style & Architecture

When writing or modifying TypeScript code, follow:

- [`docs/standards/typescript-style.md`](../../docs/standards/typescript-style.md):
  keep strict types and named exports, prefer simple interfaces and `unknown`
  over `any`, use TypeScript's standard module system, and enforce the codebase
  with the compiler, ESLint, and Prettier.
- [`docs/standards/architecture.md`](../../docs/standards/architecture.md): the
  Clean Architecture dependency rule — dependencies point inward only; the
  domain never depends on adapters, drivers, or frameworks; cross-layer work
  goes through ports implemented in outer layers and wired at the composition
  root.

Validate with `tsc --noEmit`, `eslint .`, `prettier --check .`, and the
configured test runner before committing once the TypeScript toolchain exists.
